{"title":"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is divided into four identical smaller squares, which are further divided into triangles, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What fraction of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is shaded?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d72e39255a70df70e4b40d3ece084f0d9c413e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac14 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{15}{42} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{7}{16} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac38 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"389\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Each_Value_of_X.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Each_Value_of_X)\">Solution 1 (Each Value of X)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Each Value of X)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> of the small squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dbaa7bcbcc129e8efc76dbce04421b1047eb3577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is shaded in. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f97233850e8c45f3e105cc78c27cc118c4a211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{6}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the small circles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is shaded in. This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/4369ed778c60ab5ec6a8de156a15ee5f69821e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In total, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1b86c5a2ec778195bdc893228f9d0ea0c1cffb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{16} + \\frac{1}{16} = \\frac{6 + 1}{16} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } \\frac{7}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"230\" height=\"49\" /> of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is shaded.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>